## Delivery

Commit your work on your worktree's own branch before you report. Do not merge, do not push to any other branch, do not touch another worktree: your branch is the whole delivery, and what happens to it afterwards is the office's business, not yours.

{{ROLE_BRANCH_NOTE}}

## Reporting

- Report exactly once, using the IDs and capability injected into your terminal by Orca. Follow that preamble literally; never supply Run, server or terminal identity of your own.
- Encode failure in `--outcome failed`, never in prose alone.
- List every path you touched in `--files-modified`. A path outside your write set rejects the delivery.
- Do not dispatch sub-workers. If you try, Orca refuses with `nested_worker_depth_exceeded`; complete the task yourself.

